          "text": "Clinical Indication  \nFocal epilepsy with focal impaired awareness seizures, onset at age 25, occurring approximately twice yearly. Immune-mediated etiology associated with causative LGI1 antibody. Seizures are drug responsive. Current antiseizure medication: carbamazepine.\n\nTechnique  \nRoutine digital scalp EEG recorded using electrodes placed according to the International 10–20 system and reviewed in standard montages.\n\nFindings  \nNo EEG waveform findings were provided for interpretation. Accordingly, background organization and the presence or absence of interictal epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures cannot be assessed.\n\nImpression  \nIndeterminate routine EEG due to unavailable electrographic findings. No EEG-based conclusions regarding epileptiform abnormalities or ictal localization can be made.",
